    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes `POST /api/owners` (and any owner read) return a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names. Two edits, following the project's existing OpenAPI-generated-DTO + MapStruct idiom:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. The DTO field is code-generated from this spec, so `OwnerDto.displayName` now exists on every owner response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` computing `displayName` as `lastName + \", \" + firstName` from the stored `Owner`. This flows through the create response, `getOwner`, and the list endpoints since they all go through this mapper.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` (creates an owner, then asserts `$.displayName == \"LastName, John\"`) passes, and the full test suite is green.",
